sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Session as REPL / session_v4.rs
    participant Worker as worker.rs
    participant MSexps as SharedState.module_sexps
    participant ST as SharedState.symbol_tables
    participant Sched as CompileScheduler

    Note over Session,Worker: Current state: dependency publication / readiness protocol is split across session_v4.rs, worker.rs, and scheduler.rs.

    alt Worker discovers dep during handle_import
        Worker->>ST: read dep presence / import visibility
        Worker->>MSexps: write dep sexps
        Worker->>Sched: register_module(dep, delays_other=true)
        Worker->>Sched: block_for_typecheck(caller, dep)
        Sched-->>Worker: return Blocked
    else REPL/session retries blocked dep
        Session->>MSexps: maybe write dep sexps again
        Session->>Sched: maybe register_module(dep, true) again
        Session->>Sched: wait_module_inmem_complete_blocking(dep)
    end

    par Typecheck worker path
        Worker->>ST: ensure_module_exists(dep)
        Worker->>ST: populate symbol table entries
        Worker->>Sched: notify_symbol_typechecked(...)
        Worker->>Sched: notify_typecheck_done(dep)
    and Reader fast path
        Worker->>Sched: is_typechecked(dep)?
        Sched-->>Worker: yes / no
        Worker->>ST: register_imports from dep table
    end

    Note over Sched,ST: Reader correctness depends on publication discipline spanning scheduler readiness and symbol-table completeness.
    Note over Session,MSexps: Session-side and worker-side paths each participate in publish-before-register.
    Note over Worker,Sched: Known risk surface: observed H6 residue on import fast path.
